# VNI IELTS AI — project context

> **Canonical source of truth is `docs/`.** These Cursor rules cover editor-time coding conventions only. Architecture, domain rules, and decisions live in `docs/` and are not repeated here. When this file and `docs/` disagree, `docs/` wins.

AI-powered IELTS examination platform for VNI Education. Targets: learner Web, Android, iOS, Admin CMS, and a central backend API.

## Current phase

**Phase 1 — UI/UX. There is no application code yet, and that is intentional.**

Do not scaffold projects, create `.csproj` or `package.json`, or write feature code until requirements are frozen. See `docs/development/roadmap.md`.

The HTML prototype lives outside this repository and is plain HTML/CSS/JavaScript — **no React exists yet**, despite ADR-0002 selecting it.

## Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Backend | .NET 10 / ASP.NET Core, modular monolith |
| Clients | Capacitor 8 + React + TypeScript (one source, four targets) |
| Database | MongoDB now → PostgreSQL after requirement freeze |
| AI provider | **LLM: GPT (OpenAI) + Gemini (Google) — selected 2026-08-20; Claude API excluded. Speech-to-text undecided (M-26)** |

## Invariants that constrain code

Stated here because they change what you write. Rationale is in `docs/`.

1. **Exam timing is server-authoritative.** Client timers display; they never decide. → `docs/decisions/0007-server-authoritative-exam-timer.md`
2. **AI output is never trusted application state.** Validate against a schema before use. → `docs/ai/output-contracts.md`
3. **Uploaded ZIPs are untrusted input.** Validate before extracting. → `docs/security/zip-ingestion-security.md`
4. **IELTS band tables are configuration, not code.** → `docs/domain/band-scoring.md`
5. **No AI provider type in the domain layer.** Ports in `Application`, adapters in `Infrastructure`. → `docs/decisions/0005-ai-provider-abstraction.md`
6. **No AI credentials in this repository, ever** — keys live in environment configuration. Testing routes through a third-party `baseURL` reseller with **synthetic data only**. If a task requires a live AI call, stop and say so.
7. **Domain entities carry no persistence attributes.** → `docs/decisions/0004-persistence-abstraction-boundary.md`
8. **Reading and Listening band scores come from the answer key, never from a model.** AI may generate an explanation; the explanation can never change a band. → `docs/requirements/confirmed.md` A-11
9. **Full Test and Single Skill are different modes.** Full Test: "Next" advances to the next skill *in the same session* (Reading → Listening → Writing → Speaking). Single Skill: the CTA is "new test", and it never auto-advances. → `docs/requirements/confirmed.md` E-11…E-13

## Marking uncertainty

Never resolve an ambiguity silently. Tag it: `[ASSUMPTION]` · `[OPEN QUESTION]` · `[NEEDS VALIDATION]` · `[TECHNICAL RISK]` · `[BUSINESS DECISION]`

Owner-blocking items go to `docs/requirements/assumptions-and-open-questions.md`.

Requirements and technology choices additionally carry exactly one status — `CONFIRMED` · `EXISTING` · `PROPOSED` · `UNCONFIRMED`. Canonical definitions and source precedence: `docs/README.md`. **Do not infer a requirement from the prototype, an older document, or a third-party review.**

